  "authoringNote": "C09 regression: drafts are usable for R01, R03 and R05 and only R04 requires final status. R03 reads both current usable orders: they state different order dates and different signed dates, so R03.orders_disagree holds for order.date and for order.signature_date, each naming A and B; R03 is conflict, administrative reviewer, parent set empty, citing nine facts of each order. R04 reads only final current usable documents (C09); under recorded ruling 1, a rule also cites only the documents it reads, so R04 cites the encounter and order A (six) and does not cite draft B. The only pair (E, A) is sequenced with equal identifiers, a final order exists so R04.order_not_final does not hold, and B's earlier date creates no order_before_encounter or R04 orders_disagree: R04 passes. R05 is order-centred and includes the draft: A's receipt follows the span end 2026-09-02T12:00Z and B's receipt follows 2026-08-16T12:00Z, so R05 passes citing both receipts and both order dates (eight). R01 cites both codes (nine), R02 ten, R06 five, R07 one. State needs_human_review.",
